# The new windows.yml step, run locally on 2026-11-27 before its first CI run.
#
# The step gives the windows job a CUDA toolkit and compiles the CUDA template
# with nvcc there. The job could not do that before: windows-latest ships no
# toolkit, so build.bat built the CPU shim in every earlier run of that job.
#
# What ran here is the command of the workflow, from a .cmd so that cmd's own
# redirection is not rewritten by the shell that starts it:
#
#   rmdir /s /q templates\minimal-cuda-ofx\build
#   where ninja >nul 2>&1 || python -m pip install --quiet ninja
#   set "CPU_ONLY="
#   set "CMAKE_GENERATOR=Ninja"
#   templates\minimal-cuda-ofx\build.bat
#   testkit\check-ofx-artifact.bat <bundle>\Contents\Win64\MinimalCudaGain.ofx --cuda --strict
#
# The machine: Windows 11, BuildTools 18 with MSVC 19.44 and 19.50, CUDA 12.9 and
# 13.0 installed. It differs from a runner in the one way that matters: the
# toolkit is already here, so the `Jimver/cuda-toolkit` action (v0.2.36, CUDA
# 12.9.1) is not replayed by this log - only the two commands after it are.

## 1. configure: Ninja, toolkit found, the CUDA language enabled

[build] CUDA toolkit: C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\v13.0
[build] generator: Ninja (no NVIDIA build customisations for the installed Visual Studio)
-- The CXX compiler identification is MSVC 19.44.35224.0
-- The CUDA compiler identification is NVIDIA 13.0.48 with host compiler MSVC 19.44.35224.0
-- Check for working CUDA compiler: .../v13.0/bin/nvcc.exe - skipped
-- CUDA architectures: 75;80;86;89;90;100;120 (default list)
-- Default gain: 1.0
-- OFX plugin : MinimalCudaGain (CUDA ON)

## 2. the artifact: exports, dependents, device code

  exports: 2 (OfxGetNumberOfPlugins, OfxGetPlugin)
  cuobjdump: ...\v13.0\bin\cuobjdump.exe
  device code: 7 cubin(s)

## 3. what this proves, and what it does not

Proved **[V]**: with a fresh build directory and the Ninja generator, `build.bat`
configured CMake with the CUDA language, compiled `Kernel.cu` with nvcc 13.0.48,
produced a bundle whose `.ofx` exports the two entry points and carries 7 cubins
(one per architecture in the default list), and `check-ofx-artifact.bat --cuda
--strict` exited 0.

Not proved here: that a runner image finds the toolkit the action installs (CUDA
12.9.1, not the 13.0 used above), that the runner's MSVC is one nvcc 12.9 accepts
(19.44 was, on this machine; the Ninja path pins 14.4x through `vcvars64
-vcvars_ver`, and a runner with only a newer toolset would say so rather than
compile), and - the point of the step - that no kernel ran: it never executes
`test\gpu-kernel-test.cu`.
